    </p>
    <h2>Who it is for</h2>
    <p>
      People who have just bought their first plant, people who have killed
      a few and want to know why, and anyone who wants a straight answer to
      a specific question — how often to water a snake plant, whether a ZZ
      plant really copes with low light, or what to do about brown leaf tips.
    </p>
    <h2>How the content is researched</h2>
    <p>
      Every guide is written by Zeeshan Farooq from general horticultural
      knowledge and checked against public references from university
      extension services and botanical gardens. We do not copy content from
      other websites. When a topic is genuinely debated — for example,
      whether misting helps humidity — we say so rather than pretending
      there is one settled answer. See our
      <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a> for the full
      process.
    </p>
    <h2>What this site is not</h2>
    <p>
      We are not a nursery, we do not sell plants, and we are not a
      substitute for professional advice. Our guides cover common houseplants
      and common problems; unusual or valuable plants may need specialist
      care. If you have a question or think a guide is wrong, please
      <a href="/contact/">contact us</a> — corrections are welcome.
    </p>
